# License headers

This codebase has **two** license headers and they are NOT interchangeable. Each file has the one that matches its origin. When editing: preserve it exactly. When creating a new file: pick the correct one from the decision rule below.

## Decision rule

| File class | Header | Why |
|---|---|---|
| Stub `index.php` in any sub-directory (redirect-and-exit, anti-directory-listing) | **PrestaShop SA / OSL-3.0** | PrestaShop core boilerplate. Same content PrestaShop itself ships. Keep as-is. |
| All other substantive PHP (`cdiscount.php`, `classes/*.php`, `controllers/*.php`, `functions/*.php`, `includes/*.php`, `upgrade/upgrade-*.php`, etc.) | **Feed.biz / Common-Services Commercial** | Proprietary module code authored by Feed.biz and sold under commercial license. |

How to tell if a file is a "stub `index.php`": it lives in a sub-directory, its only logic is `header('Location: ../'); exit;` (plus cache headers), and its filename is literally `index.php`. The module root's own `index.php` is also this class.

