## Rules

- **Never** replace Header A with Header B, or vice versa, on an existing file. The attribution must match the origin of the code.
- **Never** shorten, translate, reformat, or strip either header.
- **Never** stack both headers in one file.
- When splitting or moving code out of an existing file, the new file gets the same header as the one it came from.
- Keep the `@author` line as-is on existing files. On a brand-new Feed.biz-header file, set `@author` to the current author.
- The `if (!defined('_PS_VERSION_')) { exit(...); }` guard belongs right after Header B. Header A does not need it (the stub redirects before any PrestaShop code runs).
